# rm396, the skipper's unfinished plait (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm396
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for cty_kell_reedwade
written_by codex
title the skipper's unfinished plait
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk runs_a_thumb_over_an_unfinished_flat_plait
likes plum_tart knots sharp_knife misty_dawns
dislikes waiting smoke
fears losing_a_private_hope_to_public_bets
hopes enough_saved_to_choose_in_quiet
topics pastimes +0.6 travel +0.5 work +0.4 prices +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# runs a thumb across a flat three-strand plait, hums a marching air under the breath, and refuses to name the thing the saved coins might buy.

words
oath! = Fray my neat plait | Sink the spare cork
saying! = A plait has two ends | Money can keep quiet
flatwork = a flat plait | a three-strand band
shorttail = the stubby end | a short grey tail
seamknife = a narrow sharp blade | a knife with a blunt back
tartbit = a sticky plum corner | a purple half-moon of pastry
fogline = a lead-grey outline | a faint pale streak
shorepin = a fixed shore mark | a bare rock point
firstbeat = a low heel beat | a long marching note
bagmouth = the mouth of a purse | a little leather opening
linenrag = a strip of linen | a square of coarse cloth
coinceil = a saved copper | a small brass coin
smallcoil = a coil no wider than a paw | a close loop
ropepath = the right-hand strand | the upper strand
binder = a little whipping | a flat final binding
woodcheck = a pale line in wood | a dark split in grain
mistdrop = a bead of fine mist | a little hanging pearl
waitingrail = a smooth low rail | a square elbow rest

grown
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A seller can quote a fair figure without also requesting command of my intentions.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : A route looks quite different from the end where somebody's still expecting you.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : A stranger gets plain directions. My purse doesn't get opened as part of the demonstration.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : A city gets a great deal of credit for things that came in already made aboard boats.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : There should be some supper to land on after a whole day's weather has taken the expected one.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A quiet prayer needs no more room between my teeth than the first note of an old tune.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : Give me just enough of the music to keep time. Somebody else can have the crush.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Every experienced pair of hands once needed to see where the first strand went.
line @1 greet : Take the easy side. My pockets need no introduction.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : There's an unclaimed slice of bench you can see.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Sound carries well before the day gets its boots on.
line @1 greet.return : I've let the tune run on inside my head.
line @2 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Finishing this turn before my fingers can spare a nod.
line @3 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A known step fits the old tune nicely.
line @1 again.open : We've come round to the same end of the coil.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I've a bit more room set aside for a familiar shoulder.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here by the unfinished piece.
line @1 farewell : Go steady where the landing changes underfoot.
line @1 farewell.return : I hope you come in before the last note's done.
line @1 react.news : I'll see where the first strand of that came from.
line @1 react.news.known : I recognise the lay of those words already.
line @1 react.news.new : Another strand where I'd only counted two.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That account would pull crooked with a very small weight on it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I could take a turn at whatever needs doing for the hurt household.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : There's a tune I could hum with a lighter foot for that.
line @1 answer.how : A trifle worn in the joints. They still know the figure.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Working, with just enough spare time for a civil sentence.
line @1 ask.how : Is anything chafing where the day's work pulls?
line @1 decline : Those savings and their purpose both belong inside my private purse.
line @1 accept_decline : We'll leave that end loose and come away.
line @1 thank : You took the pull without tightening the wrong loop.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had a thumb free at the necessary moment.
line @1 reassure : One strand at a time will let the whole thing loosen.
line @1 sympathise : You needn't hold the heavy end alone until it's sorted.
line @1 ack : I can follow the way that piece crosses.
line @1 preclose : The loose ends are beginning to outnumber my fingers.
line @1 accept_preclose : No need to keep my tune company on your account.
line @1 offer : I could hold it level while you find the proper end.
line @1 give.advice : See where the strand first crossed before you pull on anything.
scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=knots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A flat plait will lie beside the skin without arguing at every step.
b : Do the ends need an unusual knot? | Can you recover a missed crossing?
a : Three strands kept level. The end knot's where a little argument tends to reappear. | Set it flat and see which strand hasn't had its turn. My fingers remember better than my tongue.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I hang a short length where a learner can practise without putting anything dear on the line.
b : Why not start with a real load? | What do you want taught first?
a : A mistake should only embarrass a paw at first. A full load would take a louder interest. | Letting the thing go again. There are a surprising number of ways to make two ropes hate each other permanently.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a shore mark that looks different when I've gone past it.
b : Wouldn't a bright mark do? | What will mist let you see?
a : Bright tells me where to look. A different silhouette tells me where I've got to. | I give the mark more room and move less quickly. Mist can make a very neat liar of a familiar rock.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A misty start leaves the far water undecided for a little while.
b : Does a skipper like uncertainty? | How far out can you see?
a : For admiring, yes. For giving orders I'll wait until there's a fact or two in view. | Far enough to know the limit of my sight. I try to keep that distance shorter than my claims.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a resemblance between a well-crimped tart and a well-finished rope end.
b : Should I pull on the tart? | Does the resemblance improve the taste?
a : I'd consider that wilful waste of a good crimp. Break it across the soft middle. | It gives me the pleasure of admiring it twice before I eat the bit that proves me right.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a little money by without telling it what to call itself in company.
b : Saving for a boat? | Why keep the object secret?
a : A coin asked to confirm that would have to speak, which mine stubbornly decline to do. | I want the choice to be mine even if my mind changes while the purse is filling.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pass a learner a crosswise plait with one error left in it.
b : Should you show the right one first? | Do you point to the error?
a : Side by side, yes. A hand remembers the difference in pull better than it remembers a speech about rightness. | Only after the fingers have gone looking. It takes separate skill just to see a problem clearly.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fatigue turns the tune under my breath slower before it changes what I'm doing.
b : Do you sing louder to stay awake? | When do you call a halt?
a : I listen instead for the drag and put the exacting job somewhere safe before I forget why I meant to. | When the marching tune becomes one long shuffling foot. My crew of fingers has voted.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum a marching air with no particular desire to march after anybody.
b : What do you like about it? | Remember much of the verse?
a : A reliable beat. The feet can keep it while the mind goes where it pleases. | A few. The tune generally gets better treatment without my help above a whisper.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I roll this bit of plait flat before putting it in a drawer.
b : Can't you let a drawer have some disorder? | What if it won't stay flat?
a : Of course. Most of the rest have earned the privilege through long service. | Then the error's inside the work. A drawer lid won't put manners into a twisted strand.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Waiting turns pleasant when my fingers have three loose ends of equal length.
b : And if they haven't? | What are you making while you wait?
a : Shorten the longest or spend a few very solemn minutes working out a reason not to. | The wait smaller. Selling the resulting bit of string would be an unexpected benefit.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can pray in the gap where an old marching song expects its loudest note.
b : Isn't that peculiar timing? | What do you say?
a : It leaves a memorable space. My thoughts might wander otherwise. | What belongs there that day. A prayer doesn't have to be printed on the outside of my teeth.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull on a post can appear extraordinarily important when the rest of the coast is in mist.
b : Would you steer by the gull? | What gives the truth away?
a : Only if I fancied a landmark free to leave on personal business. | The coast doesn't scratch its nose with a foot. At least I have yet to see such a coastline.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend can ask about my savings once without making it an evening's work.
b : How will a friend know to stop? | Would you lend coin to a friend?
a : I'll say the reason is private, just as I would to a stranger. A friend generally believes I mean it. | Out of another pocket if I can. Lending the hope is a different agreement altogether.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a pinched week I may set by one half of what I'd planned.
b : Does the hope shrink too? | Would you take from the purse to eat?
a : No. The calendar lengthens. I can manage that with a quieter tune and an occasional grumble. | Certainly. My future plans depend on the continued existence of an interested belly.

scene travel_2
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sharp edge at the right time is kinder to a tired rope than sawing at it with bad steel.
b : Why not mend every rope? | Who keeps the blade?
a : Sometimes the chafed part needs to go so both sound ends can take a decent new binding. | Whoever has both the task and a safe place to put it down afterwards. I like those two together.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke and sea mist part company as soon as I take a breath.
b : Which do you trust? | How far away can you tell?
a : Mist to be itself and smoke to be somebody's fire. Neither one offers much beyond its edges. | I can't always. One fine reason to give a confident explanation a moment's more travel.

scene food_2
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my slice from the side with the darker purple mark. | A plum tart that leaks in one spot is generally advertising the best bite.
b : Isn't the pastry spoilt there?
a : If it's sodden all through, yes. One little purple streak is a legitimate invitation. | Only if you're measuring pastry in terms of how well it would hold lamp oil.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can remember which hand first made a knot feel easy, without remembering the speech that came with it.
b : Can you repeat the lesson? | What does your hand remember?
a : Slowly. My learning depended rather heavily on being able to stop the teacher's fingers halfway. | The weight of the free end under the nail. Once I'd felt that, the rope seemed to explain itself.

scene work_3
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum a different beat for mending than for getting a load away.
b : Do you choose the tune? | Can others hear it?
a : The task generally picks from the shelf. A hurry has no business choosing a tune for a repair. | If anybody hears it from shore I'm exerting myself far beyond my wishes.

scene health_2
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sleepy thumbs and sharp blades ought to spend separate evenings.
b : Do you put work off? | Why not drink something strong?
a : A cut made tomorrow with steady eyes will take less time overall than patching the damage tonight. | I'd prefer all ten fingers to be making their own decisions.

scene prices_2
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little saved coin can make a loud noise in an otherwise empty pocket.
b : Afraid it will be heard? | Do you wrap your coins?
a : More weary of explaining than afraid. A bit of cloth can save a great many clever remarks. | The savings, yes. A coin bound on an errand may ring out its ambitions freely.

scene friends_2
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A meal tastes better after someone has shown me a trick I didn't know.
b : Even if it proves you wrong? | What would you offer to teach back?
a : Especially. Taking one's pride down a notch can improve the appetite. | A flat plait or a neat finish. Eating the tart comes quite naturally without a demonstration.

scene day_2
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hate being kept waiting on a decision already made. | An hour awaiting clear water costs less temper than a minute waiting for an answer somebody knows.
b : Would you demand an answer?
a : I'd ask if the decision was made. A quiet yes saves both parties the exhibition of my patience. | If it concerns the safety of a crew, plainly. If it concerns a price, I've feet to walk elsewhere.

scene smalltalk_2
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tie my purse with a fussy little tuck on dull days. | An awkward purse string has prevented me making some very convenient purchases.
b : On purpose?
a : Mainly for the pleasure of undoing it. I don't want the days getting all their interest from the coin inside. | The first time was an accident. The second knot was a deliberate intervention on behalf of my hope.

scene travel_3
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good landing has some way to climb out with stiff legs and a wet sleeve.
b : What else would you put there? | Do you mind a rough view?
a : A clear spot where another traveller can wait without pressing down on the first pair of hands. | If I can land safely, I'll let the view attend to its own grooming.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd teach a new arrival one simple knot worth remembering rather than impress anyone with seven.
b : Which one? | What if the first try fails?
a : The one that will hold the newcomer's own bundle and can be untied with cold fingertips. | Take it apart. The rope is a patient audience if I resist explaining its entire family history.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The tale come ashore is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Is it holding together? | Would you send it back out?
a : Under its own weight, perhaps. I wouldn't hang a reputation from it just yet. | I would first want to see where the teller has joined a guess onto the fact.

story secret [topic=memories]
  : I put a coin away in a rag and forgot which rag I'd used.
  : On washday four little parcels sat in a row looking equally prosperous.
  b : Did you open them all?
  : I weighed them on my palm and went straight to the heavy one. It was a knot of old sinkers. I've since improved my bookkeeping.

story plait [topic=pastimes]
  : I made a long neat plait out of three scraps and held it up with some pride.
  : I'd woven the middle strand straight through a buttonhole on my coat.
  b : Did you have to cut it free?
  : I wore my handiwork home. Nobody asked to buy it in that particular arrangement.

story whistle [topic=work]
  : I tried giving the marching tune a whistle instead of a hum while my hands were busy.
  : The final note went astonishingly high just as I leaned over a board.
  b : Did it startle you?
  : My pocket had caught on a nail. The tune had acquired one extremely enthusiastic wind instrument.

story tarts [topic=food]
  : I used a flat strand to tie two little tart boxes together for a walk.
  : The knot travelled less well than the pastry and both boxes arrived in one rather intimate heap.
  b : Were the tarts ruined?
  : A sweet success with the forks. I only had to give up my intention of presenting them as separate gifts.

story distant [topic=weather]
  : A point in the mist once looked so exactly like a familiar high post that I almost greeted it by name.
  : Then it began to bob very slowly sideways.
  b : A boat?
  : A twig a few lengths from my foot. A most profitable reminder that fog leaves distance off the account.

rule @plait
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Centre strand over and let the shorter end breathe. | Nothing clever needed till the ends ask to be finished.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep one certain point inside the grey. | No hurry to name a hull through that veil.

rule @early
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A marching tune suits the waking fingers. | Good hour for a quiet count of sound strands.

rule @trade
when concept=bark self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the loaded end room before handling the slack. | A firm landing is worth a little extra circuit.

rule @teach
when concept=bark self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the learner feel which turn is pulling crooked. | Nobody learns much by watching my knuckles go fast.

rule @coin
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the pocket quiet a little longer. | A private purchase needn't name itself in advance.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I can keep one ear open while my fingers plait.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your particular step needs no introduction.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Speak to the matter and keep the purse out of it.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Soft voices carry well before the wind starts moving.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=sailor] : At #self.workplace# I prefer to test the loose end before anybody relies on the tight one.
dlg @2 resident.job : I do well with work that gives a steady pair of fingers a reason for showing up.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : These words held together as far as this bench. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The strand I've heard says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I wouldn't call the whole rope tested.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Go out with a sound loop and enough slack for the turn.
dlg @1 master.work : Hands learn by touching the mistake and undoing it. A perfect piece kept behind glass will teach you remarkably little.
dlg @1 master.wages : No wages for learning. Working here beside me speeds your learning threefold. The pieces you produce are yours for selling.
dlg @1 master.bye : Loosen the practice knot before your fingers grow tired of it.
graft resident.hub
choice What's the plait for? -> plait_purpose
node plait_purpose
say To keep my fingers moving in a pattern I can trust while I think about a different one. It might make a fine purse tie in due time.
choice What will the purse buy? -> plait_private
choice I'll stay with the plait. -> hub
node plait_private
say There you have jumped from inspecting the rope to demanding the ship's cargo. I'll gladly show you the first crossing again.
choice I'll stay with the plait. -> hub

graft master.learn
choice Can you show me where a knot went wrong? -> plait_wrong
node plait_wrong
say Lay it on something level. Move the free end a very little, and watch which turn grows tight instead of slack.
choice What should I move first? -> plait_slack
choice I'll try the free part. -> learn
node plait_slack
say The part still willing to budge. A battle with the tightest turn usually provides a very expensive lesson about fingernails.
choice I'll try the free part. -> learn
